<p class="eyebrow"><a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> / Dashboard</p>
<h1>Every call, message, and recording from your VoiceML account.</h1>
<p class="lede">The VoiceML Dashboard collects the voicemail, recordings, and transcripts your call flows produce, emails each recipient a secure link, and gives operators a live switchboard with call control. Sign in with Google; nothing to install.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ site.voicemlDashboardUrl }}">Sign in to the dashboard</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/voiceml/">Explore VoiceML</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How it works</h2>
	<p>Point a VoiceML callback at the dashboard with the recipient's email address in the URL. The dashboard keeps the complete payload, downloads the recording, and emails the recipient a summary with a link to that one message. Related recording and transcript callbacks are joined into a single message.</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>&lt;Response&gt;
  &lt;Say&gt;Please leave a message after the tone.&lt;/Say&gt;
  &lt;Record
    recordingStatusCallback="{{ site.voicemlDashboardUrl }}/voicemail/you%40example.com"
    recordingStatusCallbackEvent="completed"
    transcribe="true"
    transcribeCallback="{{ site.voicemlDashboardUrl }}/transcript/you%40example.com"/&gt;
&lt;/Response&gt;</code></pre>
	<p>Use <code>/recording/</code> for call recordings, <code>/voicemail/</code> for voicemail, <code>/transcript/</code> for transcripts, and <code>/status/</code> for call status callbacks. Callback URLs can also carry call context, such as the digits a caller pressed, which the dashboard shows with the message.</p>
